WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.400
Hi. Today,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.960
we're going to show you how
to connect GitHub Copilot to an

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.025
RStudio project on Posit Cloud.

00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:14.225
The first thing to do is
create a new RStudio project.

00:00:14.225 --> 00:00:15.825
And when the
project is loading,

00:00:15.825 --> 00:00:19.730
we can go ahead and give
it a name. Maybe AI Coding Assistant.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.390
And then as soon as
the project loads,

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.810
we're gonna go ahead and
authenticate through GitHub.

00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:31.035
To do that, you're gonna
click Tools on the navigation bar,

00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:33.115
then Global Options,

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.110
scroll down to Copilot,

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.030
and you can enable
GitHub Copilot.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:42.230
First, you're going to install
some packages in the IDE.

00:00:43.655 --> 00:00:44.935
Once this is ready,

00:00:44.935 --> 00:00:47.195
you're going to be able
to sign in now to GitHub.

00:00:48.135 --> 00:00:49.655
So if you click on this button,

00:00:49.655 --> 00:00:52.455
it's going to give you a
verification code. You can copy

00:00:52.455 --> 00:00:55.710
that. And take it
to a GitHub link.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.390
Paste in the verification
code. Click continue.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.350
Authorize GitHub Copilot.

00:01:03.495 --> 00:01:05.755
Now you're done here.
You can close this tab

00:01:06.775 --> 00:01:08.235
and come back into the IDE.

00:01:09.655 --> 00:01:12.980
This will update and it'll show
you that you are now logged in

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.840
and ready to use Copilot.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.280
So we can open up a new
script to show it off.

00:01:21.695 --> 00:01:23.235
Maybe I'll rename that

00:01:23.945 --> 00:01:25.155
eda.R.

00:01:26.095 --> 00:01:28.975
And we can start passing
in, you know, human language text.

00:01:28.975 --> 00:01:30.035
Right? Make a function

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.440
that's going to calculate
the area of a room.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.220
You can click enter,

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.800
and you're gonna see
the recommendation from GitHub Copilot.

00:01:40.745 --> 00:01:42.905
You can click tab to
accept the recommendation,

00:01:42.905 --> 00:01:43.705
and you can run it,

00:01:43.705 --> 00:01:46.045
and now you have a
function `area()` in your environment.

00:01:46.745 --> 00:01:48.960
You can also ask it
to say, you know,

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.960
I have a room of
a certain size,

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.280
find out the area of the floor,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.000
and it's going to know that
it's going to take the formula

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.355
that I just defined,

00:01:57.355 --> 00:02:00.715
and be able to run this and
find out that the area is in

00:02:00.715 --> 00:02:02.735
fact eighty for my size room.

00:02:03.595 --> 00:02:05.530
I can also use, like,
an auto complete.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.290
So let's load in ggplot2.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:13.150
And if I start
typing the function `ggplot()` here,

00:02:13.725 --> 00:02:16.205
you're going to see that it's
gonna start filling it in for

00:02:16.205 --> 00:02:17.585
me with some, you
know, recommendations.

00:02:18.685 --> 00:02:19.005
Okay.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.825
Let's just go ahead and accept this
and see what it comes up with.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.990
You know, a pretty
basic first ggplot.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:28.550
But then you can work with
it again with human language and

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:29.430
say things like, well,

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:33.185
maybe I wanna change the
color of the data points.

00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:37.105
It would do that
based on the variable class.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.750
We can accept this and run it.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.250
And now we've got, you know,
a slightly improved graphic,

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.775
and you can keep iterating on
this using Copilot to help you

00:02:50.775 --> 00:02:53.595
out make new things and
hopefully make them faster.

